completeLinearSystemOnNodalPlaneCurve -- Compute the complete linear system of a divisor on a nodal plane curve
***************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        (L,h)=completeLinearSystemOnNodalPlaneCurve(I,D)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, of a nodal plane curve C,
      * D, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, \{D_0,D_1\}\ of ideals
        representing effective divisors on C
  * Outputs:
      * L, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, of homogeneous forms with 1
        row and with number of columns equal to $h^0(D_0-D_1)$
      * h, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, such that
        L_{(0,i)}/h represents a basis of $H^0 O(D_0-D_1)$

Description
===========

Compute the complete linear series of D_0-D_1 on the normalization of C via
adjoint curves and double linkage.

