distinctPlanePoints -- Generates the ideal of k random points in the coordinate ring $R$ of $\\P^{ 2}$
******************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        (random distinctPlanePoints)(k,R)
  * Inputs:
      * k, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the number of points
      * R, a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, the
        homogeneous coordinate ring of $\mathbb{P}^2$
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the vanishing ideal of the points

Description
===========

Creates the ideal of the points via a random choice of their Hilbert-Burch
matrix, which is taken to be of generic shape.

+---------------------------------------------+
|i1 : setRandomSeed("alpha");                 |
| -- setting random seed to 10206284518       |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R=ZZ/32003[x_0..x_2];                   |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i3 : Ipts=(random distinctPlanePoints)(10,R);|
|                                             |
|o3 : Ideal of R                              |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i4 : betti res Ipts                          |
|                                             |
|            0 1 2                            |
|o4 = total: 1 5 4                            |
|         0: 1 . .                            |
|         1: . . .                            |
|         2: . . .                            |
|         3: . 5 4                            |
|                                             |
|o4 : BettiTally                              |
+---------------------------------------------+

For the programmer
==================

The object *note distinctPlanePoints: distinctPlanePoints, is an instance of
the type *note RandomObject: (RandomObjects)RandomObject,.

